1]Explain what is operator ? and types of operators in java ?

	->An operator is a symbol which is used to perform operations
	->In java thier are 6 different types of operators:-
		1]Arithematic Operators 
		2]Assignment Operator
		3]Relational Operators
		4]Logical Operators 
		5]Ternary Operator
		6]Unary Operators   
		 
		
->Arithematic Operators:-
	1]Arithematic operators are used to perform arithematic operations between 2 operands
	2]In arithematic operators thier are symbols like +,-,*,/ and %
	
->Assignment Operator:-
	1]Assignment operator is used to assign a value to an variable
	2]In assignment operator thier is only one symbol "=",we can also use arithematic operators along with
	the assignment operator
	

->Relational Operators:-
	1]Relational operators are used to compare the values of 2 operands and return boolean ie.. true or false
	2]In Relational operators their are symbols like >,<,>=,<=,== and !=
	

->Logical Operators:-
	1]Logical Operators is used to combine multiple boolean expressions and evaluate the overall result
	as true or false
	2]In Logical operators thier are Logical AND,Logical OR and LogicalNOT
	3]In LogicalAND both the conditions must be true then only it will give the output as true
	4]In LogicalOR if any one condition is true then it will give the output as true
	5]LogicalNOT will simply reverse the boolean value,if it is true then it will make it as false
	if it is false then it will make it as true.
	
	
->Ternary Operator:-
	1]In java ternary operator is a concise way to express if-else statement,it is also known as 
	conditional statement.
	

->Unary Operators:-
	1]Unary Operators perform on single operand
	2]In unary operators their are symbols like +,-,! and incrementation/decrementation
	

	Incrementation
	--------------
		i)Incrementation is the process of incrementing the value by 1
		ii)In incrementation thier are 2 types:-
			1]Post incrementation
			2]Pre incrementation
			
		->Post incrementation is the process of using the value first and then incrementing the value by 1
		->Pre incrementation is the process of incrementing the value by 1 and using it
		->for both post and pre incrementation we use ++ symbol
		
	Decrementation
	--------------
		i)Decrementation is the process of decrementing the value by 1
		ii)In decrementation thier are 2 types:-
			1]Post decrementation
			2]Pre decrementation
		
		->Post decrementation is the process of using the value first and then decrementing the value by 1
		->Pre decrementation is the process of decrementing the value by 1 and then using it
		->for both post and pre decrementation we use -- symbol




2]Explain indetail about conditional statements in java ?	

	->Conditional statements are also known as decision making statements in java
	->In java thier are 5 decision making statements:-
		i)Simple if statement
		ii)if-else statement
		iii]if-else-if statement
		iv]Nested if statement
		v)switch statement
		
Simple if statement:-
====================
	1)if statement is used to test a specific condition,if the condition is true,if block code will get
	executed,if the condition is false then the control will execute the remaning statements after if
	block
	
if else statement:-
===================
	1)if else statement is used to test a specific condition,if the condition is true,if block code will
	get executed,if the condition is false then else block code will get executed.
	

if else if statement:-
======================
	1)if else if statement is used to check multiple conditions and execute the specific block of statements
	dependending upon on true condition among them.
	
	
Nested if statement:-
=====================
	1)Having if statement in another if is called as nested if statement
	2)if the first if condition is true,then only the control will enters the inner if condition
	3)if the first if condition is false then the control will execute the first if,else block statements
	4)if the inner if condition is true then only the control will execute the inner if statements
	5)if the inner if condition is false then the control will execute the inner if,else block statements 
	
	
switch statement:-
==================
	1)Switch statement is used to check multiple cases and execute the true case among them,if none of the
	case is true,then it will execute the default statement,and to prevent the control falling to the
	subsequent cases we use break.
		


3]Explain indetail about iterating statements in java ?

	->Iterating statements are also known as looping statements
	->Looping statements is used to execute the given code again and again until the specified condition
	evaluates to false
	->In java thier are 3 types of looping statements:
		i)for loop
		ii)while loop
		iii)do while loop
		

for loop:-
==========
	1]for loop keeps on executing the code until the specified sequence exhausts
	2]for loop has 3 parts:
		i)intialization
		ii)condition
		iii)incrementation/decrementation
	3]for loop is also known as entry control loop.
	

while loop:-
============
	1]while loop keeps on executing the code continously until the specified condition evaluates to false
	2]while loop is also known as entry control loop.
	
	
	
do while loop:-
===============
	1]do-while loop is similiar to while loop but it gurantees that the code present inside the loop will
	executes atleast once before the condition is tested
	2]do while loop is also known as exist control loop.




4]Explain what is break in java ?

	->Break statement is used to exist from a loop or switch statement prematurely
	->It stops the execution and transfers the control to the next statement after the loop/switch statement.




5]Explain what is continue in java ?

	->Continue statement is used to skip the current iteration of a loop
	->It does not terminates the loop but it just skips the remaining code for that iteration.




6]Explain indetail about comments in java ?

	->In java comments are used to show the purpose of the code and prevents certain lines from the execution
	->In java thier are 3 types of comments:-
		i)Single line comment
		ii)Multi line comments
		iii)Documentational comments
		
		
->Singleline comment:-
======================
	i)Single line comment is used to comment single line of code
	ii)Single comment starts with // and continues to the end of the line
	iii)The main purpose of the single line comment is to explain code in short
	

->Multiline comment:-
======================
	i)Multiline comment is used to comment multiple lines of code
	ii)Multiline comment starts with /* and ends with */
	iii)The main purpose of the multiline comment is to explain larger section of code
	
->Documentational comment:-
===========================
	i)Documentational comments are used to generate HTML documentation
	ii)Documentational comments starts with /** and ends with */


7]Explain indetail about Array in java ?

	->An array is an collection of homogeneous data elements which means an array can store only single
	type of values and arrays are treated as objects in java hence to create an array we has to make use of
	new keyword,Array stores the values in contiginous memory locations
	->Java supports different types of arrays:-
		1]2d Array
		2]Jagged Array
		3]3d Array
		
->The 2 dimensional array in java programming is an array of array,in 2d array the data can be stored in rows
and columns and we can access the index by using both row index and column index


->The jagged array is an array of array,such that members arrays can be of different sizes


->The 3d array is an collection of 2d array,The 3d array is also known as multidimensional array.
